What is Sulfate of Potash?
Sulfate of Potash (SOP), chemically known as potassium sulfate (K₂SO₄), is a premium fertilizer highly valued for its dual nutrient content of potassium and sulfur. Unlike other potassium fertilizers, SOP is completely chloride-free, making it ideal for chloride-sensitive crops such as fruits, vegetables, tobacco, and certain nuts. It enhances crop quality, improves stress resistance, and boosts yield without the risk of chloride toxicity. SOP is particularly favored in precision agriculture and organic farming systems where soil health and crop specificity are paramount.
While Muriate of Potash (MOP) remains more common due to lower costs, SOP commands a premium market position because of its specialized applications and superior performance in quality-sensitive agriculture.
